@Tripora.UserService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5001

### Scenario 1 & 5: Valid Customer Registration
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Eleanor Vance",
  "email": "eleanor.vance@tripora.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "confirmPassword": "SecurePassword123!"
}

###

### Scenario 2: Duplicate Email (Submit same email again)
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Eleanor Vance",
  "email": "eleanor.vance@tripora.com",
  "password": "AnotherPassword123!",
  "confirmPassword": "AnotherPassword123!"
}

###

### Scenario 3A: Invalid Email Format
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "ValidPassword123!",
  "confirmPassword": "ValidPassword123!"
}

###

### Scenario 3B: Weak Password (missing uppercase, number, special char)
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "email": "johndoe@example.com",
  "password": "weakpassword",
  "confirmPassword": "weakpassword"
}

###

### Scenario 3C: Mismatched Passwords
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "email": "johndoe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "confirmPassword": "DifferentPassword123!"
}

###
